@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# App
+
+## Users API
+
+The functions in `src/api/` take an in-memory `Db` (see `src/db.js`) as their first argument. Build one with `migrate(new Db())` from `src/migrate.js`.
+
+A **user** is an object with these fields:
+
+| Field       | Type             | Notes                                       |
+| ----------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
+| `id`        | string           | UUID, assigned by `createUser`              |
+| `email`     | string           | Must contain `@`; unique, ignoring case     |
+| `fullName`  | string           | Non-empty after trimming, at most 100 characters |
+| `nickname`  | string \| null   | Optional; `null` when not set               |
+| `createdAt` | string           | ISO 8601 timestamp                          |
+| `lastLogin` | string \| null   | ISO 8601 timestamp, or `null` if never set  |
+
+Every function throws `Error('<name>: db is required')` when `db` is missing.
+
+### `src/api/users.js`
+
+#### `createUser(db, { email, fullName })`
+
+Creates a user with a new `id` and the current time as `createdAt`. Returns the user.
+
+Throws if the email has no `@`, is already in use (ignoring case), or `fullName` is not a valid name.
+
+```js
+const user = createUser(db, { email: 'ada@example.com', fullName: 'Ada Lovelace' });
+```
+
+#### `getUser(db, id)`
+
+Returns the user with that `id`, or `null`.
+
+#### `getUserByEmail(db, email)`
+
+Returns the user whose email matches, ignoring case, or `null`.
+
+#### `listUsers(db, { limit = 50, offset = 0 } = {})`
+
+Returns one page of users, oldest first. Pass `{ limit: Infinity }` to get every user.
+
+#### `countUsers(db)`
+
+Returns the number of users.
+
+#### `updateUser(db, id, { email, fullName })`
+
+Changes only the fields you pass and returns the updated user. Omitted fields are kept.
+
+Throws if the user does not exist, or if a new email or `fullName` is invalid. A failed update changes nothing.
+
+#### `searchUsers(db, query)`
+
+Returns every user whose email or full name contains `query`, ignoring case, oldest first. Results are not paginated.
+
+#### `deleteUser(db, id)`
+
+Removes the user. Returns `true` if a user was removed, or `false` if no user had that `id`.
+
+#### `recordLogin(db, id, when = new Date())`
+
+Sets the user's `lastLogin` to `when` and returns the updated user.
+
+Throws if no user has that `id`.
+
+### `src/api/format.js`
+
+#### `displayName(user)`
+
+Returns `user.fullName` when it is not blank. Otherwise returns the part of `user.email` before `@`.
+
+```js
+displayName({ email: 'ada@example.com', fullName: '' }); // 'ada'
+```
+
+### `src/api/export.js`
+
+#### `exportUsersCsv(db)`
+
+Returns every user as CSV text, oldest first, with the header `id,email,fullName,createdAt,lastLogin`. Fields containing commas, quotes or line breaks are quoted. Output ends with a newline.
+
+#### `importUsersCsv(db, csv)`
+
+Reads CSV in the format `exportUsersCsv` writes, keeping each user's `id` and timestamps, and returns how many users it imported.
+
+Throws if the header or a row is invalid, or if an id or email duplicates one in the database or the file. Nothing is written unless every row is valid.
+
+## Tests
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
